    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated attack, led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchors the utility spot with a 67.11 rating. His matchup against Legumina is our strongest play; the 4.32 xERA of the opposing starter, combined with a favorable park factor and a premium #2 spot in the order, positions **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** as our primary run-production engine. Following closely is **Drake Baldwin**, whose 59.15 score is buoyed significantly by his leadoff assignment. While facing a lefty in Hart presents a neutral platoon scenario, the volume of plate appearances at the top of the lineup makes **Drake Baldwin** an essential component of today\u2019s offensive floor.\n\nEfficiency remains a concern elsewhere, forcing us to be surgical with our remaining slots. **Brayan Rocchio** earns a 44.53 score against the difficult Bradley, T; despite the SP\u2019s 3.82 xERA, **Brayan Rocchio** retains value primarily through his order placement. Meanwhile, **Dominic Smith** sits at a marginal 40.68, hampered by a lefty-on-lefty platoon disadvantage that limits his ceiling. We are keeping a close watch on **Jackson Merrill**, who narrowly missed the starting cut; his 55.75 baseline projection was neutralized by a rough matchup against Sale and a projected bottom-third lineup position, making him the odd man out to preserve game caps. We are proceeding without the high-upside contributions of **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** today due to scheduled off-days, placing increased pressure on our active quartet to maintain our standing in the 5x5 categories.",
